# XSH posix_spawnattr_getpgroup() and posix_spawnattr_setpgroup()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Effects are shown by really spawning this program as a child image. The
# functions return the error number; errno is not used.

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getpgroup.001
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getpgroup.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getpgroup.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawnattr_getpgroup() on a newly initialised object returns 0 and
           stores 0.
test       t/001-default.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getpgroup.002
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getpgroup.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getpgroup.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawnattr_setpgroup() with the caller's own process group ID
           returns 0 and posix_spawnattr_getpgroup() stores it; setting
           0 afterwards makes it read back 0; two objects keep their own
           values.
test       t/002-roundtrip.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getpgroup.003
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getpgroup.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With POSIX_SPAWN_SETPGROUP set and spawn-pgroup the ID of an existing
           process group (led by an earlier spawned child), the child
           spawned joins that group.
test       t/003-join.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getpgroup.004
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getpgroup.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With a non-zero spawn-pgroup but POSIX_SPAWN_SETPGROUP clear, the child
           stays in the parent's process group.
test       t/004-unused-without-flag.c
